From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: regulator: apple,pmic-touch-regulator: Add the
 D2089 supplies

The touchscreen of the A7 iPad Air takes an analog and a core supply
from the D2089 PMIC. Add their compatibles.

[Orchard: from thisiscamk/ipad-air-j72-linux 2a257d6,
 code/current/kernel/0001-j72-installed-kernel-snapshot.patch
 (Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/apple,pmic-touch-regulator.yaml);
 the separate analog-bias regulator and its bias-supply property are
 left out, as the driver now keeps the shared bias like on the D2207.]
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/regulator/apple,pmic-touch-regulator.yaml        | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/apple,pmic-touch-regulator.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/apple,pmic-touch-regulator.yaml
index 45521f912..f02ee8ccb 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/apple,pmic-touch-regulator.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/apple,pmic-touch-regulator.yaml
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ maintainers:
   - Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
 
 description:
-  Fixed touchscreen supply switches provided by the D2186, D2207, Adelyn,
+  Fixed touchscreen supply switches provided by the D2089, D2186, D2207, Adelyn,
   Angel, Chestnut and Acorn PMICs. The compatible identifies both the PMIC and the physical supply;
   register layout is an implementation detail of the regulator driver.
 
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@ properties:
       - apple,adelyn-touch-core-regulator
       - apple,angel-touch-analog-regulator
       - apple,chestnut-touch-hv-regulator
+      - apple,d2089-touch-analog-regulator
+      - apple,d2089-touch-core-regulator
       - apple,d2186-touch-core-regulator
       - apple,d2207-touch-analog-regulator
 
